<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">American Colonization Society</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1816</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The American Colonization Society was an organisation founded in Washington in 1816 to settle free Black Americans in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Its supporters ranged from opponents of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> to slaveholders who wished to remove free Black people from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, and it was opposed by many <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-americans">African Americans</a> and abolitionists. It founded the colony of Liberia in 1822 and helped several thousand settlers emigrate there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/american-colonization-society.jpg" alt="American Colonization Society" width="320" height="333" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Felipe Fidelis Tobias · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_American_Colonization_Society.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
